;; ask (FEAT-018 S-A) — the strict synchronous mission function.
;;
;; The 90% LLM call: spawn a child toward `prompt`, await it, return its result
;; DATA. The gather-of-one case over the await-free primitives (spawn-session +
;; await-session). Authority is GRANTED, not inferred (doc-14 Decision 5): pass
;; :tools to attenuate the child, :region to join one, :inherit-memory to seed it.
;;
;; Args (data/*):
;;   prompt          — the child's mission prompt (required).
;;   tools           — optional capability subset (clamped to this session's ceiling).
;;   region          — optional region to join (else a fresh Fork-A region).
;;   inherit-memory  — optional def-env slice to seed the child.
;;
;; Returns the child's result value (await-session unwraps {:ok v} -> v), or an
;; {"err" ...} map if the child failed.
(let [h (tool/spawn-session {:prompt data/prompt
                             :tools data/tools
                             :region data/region
                             :inherit-memory data/inherit-memory})]
  (tool/await-session {:handle h}))
